{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "f1d63753-04b6-8acb-bc88-0703d575a7a0",
  "created_at": "2026-02-05T11:10:46-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Utilities",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "David Cohen",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Priya Raman",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:04:25-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "City of Newport Utilities, this is Priya. How can I help you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:04:32-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hey, yeah, hi. David Cohen. I'm calling about my water and sewer bill, because it's wicked high this quarter and totally not right."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:04:45-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm sorry to hear that, Mr. Cohen. Can you tell me what the bill looks like compared to usual?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:04:56-05:00",
      "duration": 24,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It's like four times what it normally is. And the reason is, we had a pipe break in the basement back in, um, early January. Plumber fixed it, I've got the receipt. So I'm wondering if there's a leak adjustment or something. [line breaks up]"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:05:20-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You broke up a little at the end there. Did you say the plumber repaired it in January?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:05:30-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, early January. Pipe split, water ran for I don't know, a few days before we caught it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:05:40-05:00",
      "duration": 20,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. There is generally a process where you can request a review of the bill after a documented leak repair. You would typically need the repair invoice and the dates. Do you have the account number handy?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:06:00-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hang on. Um, the thing is, the account's not in my name. It's in my wife's name. She passed, so it never got switched over. Is that going to be a problem?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:06:17-05:00",
      "duration": 17,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I'm sorry for your loss. It's not a problem for the call, but we will want to get the account moved into your name as the homeowner. What name is it under?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:06:34-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Rachel Cohen. Same last name, obviously. Hold on, seven letters... no, sorry, I'm doing a crossword here while I wait on hold, hang on. Seven across, 'stubborn.' Anyway. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:06:50-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. I've got the account under Rachel Cohen. Is the service address the home you live in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:07:00-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, same house. I'd rather not say the street on a cell phone, the reception's garbage anyway."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:07:10-05:00",
      "duration": 16,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's all right, I can find it by the name for now. I see the account. The latest bill is quite a bit above the earlier ones, you're right."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:07:26-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Told you. So what do I do, send the receipt in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:07:33-05:00",
      "duration": 26,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. You'd send a copy of the plumber's invoice, a short note with the date of the break and the repair, and a copy of the death certificate or something showing you're the owner, so we can update the name. You can bring it to City Hall or mail it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:07:59-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Can I email it? I don't wanna drive down there."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:08:05-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I don't have an email address I can give you from here. I can transfer you to the billing office, or I can note your account that you're submitting documents. Mailing or dropping it off is the safe route."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:08:26-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Fine, mailing. Okay, and the bill itself, it's due soon. Is there a drop box at City Hall? Like if I get there after you close, can I just put a payment in?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:08:44-05:00",
      "duration": 21,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, there is a payment drop box at City Hall for after-hours payments. Checks should go in with the bill stub or your account number written on them. Also, the city has an online payment option through the website."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:09:05-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, good. Cause I work till six most days. So drop box, check, account number on it. Got it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:09:16-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Right. And if the adjustment is approved, the difference would be credited afterward, so paying the amount you can in the meantime avoids a late charge on it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:09:31-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Wicked annoying that I pay for a leak and then wait for money back, but whatever. How long does the review take?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:09:43-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "It varies, and I don't want to put a number on it. Once the documents come in, the billing staff will review and contact you. May I confirm your phone number for the account note?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:10:02-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, it's 401-555-0192."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:10:05-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four zero one, five five five, zero one nine two. Correct?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:10:12-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "That's it. [pause] Sorry, one sec. 'Obstinate.' Yes. Okay, sorry, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:10:19-05:00",
      "duration": 13,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I've added a note that you're calling about a leak review and the name change. Is there anything else I can help with today?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:10:32-05:00",
      "duration": 8,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Nope, that's it. Thanks, Priya. Totally appreciate it, even though the bill still stinks."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-05T11:10:40-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Understood. Thanks for calling, Mr. Cohen. Have a good afternoon."
    }
  ],
